{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.QuantumPressure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.QuantumPressure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.MathConstants","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.boundaryPressure_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.boundaryPressure_order","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-pressure.lean#L56-L65","doc":"The boundary pressure scales as ℏ_q²: it is a second-order quantum\ncorrection that vanishes faster than ℏ_q as q → 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.boundaryPressure_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.boundaryPressure_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-pressure.lean#L44-L54","doc":"The boundary pressure is non-negative when inputs are non-negative\nand volume is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.boundaryPressure_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.boundaryPressure_classical","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-pressure.lean#L37-L42","doc":"The boundary pressure vanishes at classicality (q = 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.boundaryPressure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.boundaryPressure","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-pressure.lean#L29-L35","doc":"**Boundary pressure correction** from the q-anomaly.\nP_boundary = ℏ_q² · ⟨d_q K, d_q K⟩ / V_q.\nThis is parameterised by the boundary pairing norm (a non-negative real).\nLabel: def:quantum-pressure ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-pressure","label":"def:quantum-pressure","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-pressure.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.R_q","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-pressure.lean#L25-L27","doc":"Ground ring: archimedean specialisation `R_q := ℝ` (AGENTS.md §7c).\nThe numerical substrate value `q₀ ≈ 1.1097` lives in `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}